WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.360
Hi, I'm Toby, and welcome back to another
video.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:10.780
Today I'd like to show you through the school
and university grades of the inventor Nikola Tesla.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:16.220
Now Tesla, maybe more than any other scientist
is regarded as being a true genius.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:21.960
He had over 300 patents in his name, and these
are responsible for much of the technology

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.880
in our world today.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.800
He was behind the use of alternating currents
which power our world, but he was also behind

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:36.850
things like radio, x-rays, wireless communication,
and he had dreams of providing the world with

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.680
wireless power.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.149
Now the story of his grades shows that he
started off really well in his first year,

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:47.899
but by his third year of university, he had
dropped out.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:55.720
Now, Tesla's life has a bit of a trend of
unfortunate circumstances getting in the way of genius.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.400
And his studies are no different.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:04.470
So although he never actually graduated, his
time as a student did lay the groundwork for

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.070
his knowledge and ideas in physics and engineering.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.060
So let's have a look at what he did.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:15.310
The first set of documents I have here are
from Tesla's time at school.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:23.349
Now, when Tesla was 14 he moved north of his
home-town to attend a Realschule in Rakovac.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:30.369
He was here for three years, from 1870 to
1873, and it's where he developed a special

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:32.479
interest in physics.

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:38.720
This first document here is part of his matriculation
certificate, that's like his graduation from

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:39.749
the school.

00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:45.810
An interesting note about it is this is actually
a duplicate, because his original document

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.859
was stolen from him on the day that he was
due to depart for America in 1884.

00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:57.359
I then have his grades from the three years
at that school, and these are a translated

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:59.559
version that I've put into a table.

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:03.960
And I got the information from the school
website which I'll put in the description.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:10.049
We've got the subject he was taking, his grade
in the first semester and his grade in the

00:02:10.049 --> 00:02:11.620
second semester.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:17.769
His overall success in his first year translated
to first row and first row with honors, which

00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:19.640
sounds like he's doing pretty well.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:25.629
We've got an excellent in Maths over here,
his diligence is persistent, and his moral

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:28.719
conduct is exemplary.

00:02:28.719 --> 00:02:30.459
Let's have a look at the second year.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:36.609
It looks fairly similar, we have physics on
here at commendable and excellent, chemistry

00:02:36.609 --> 00:02:42.420
at sufficient and excellent, his written works
are considered neat, and again his overall

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.299
success is first row.

00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:47.870
Let's have a look at his third year at this
school.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.080
Now, something interesting on his third year
grade sheet is that in math he actually has

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.310
a fail, it's insufficient.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:00.540
Now, this might not say so much about his
math skills and more about the fact that Tesla

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.481
was apparently ill for two months, which is
noted here on his absence.

00:03:04.481 --> 00:03:10.620
And if you look over to the next page which
is his matura exam, these are the last set

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.420
of exams that he would have done at this school,
he actually has an excellent in mathematics,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.799
so I don't think that it's saying Tesla was
bad at maths at school, it just seems that

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:23.810
he was unfortunately ill and probably didn't
perform as well as he wanted to there.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:29.599
Overall they consider him mature for technical
education, which means he's got a good groundwork

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:31.849
to go on and study this further.

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:35.900
During his time at this school, Tesla lived
with his aunt and uncle.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.049
I'd like to read you a quote about his time
staying there.

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:43.590
"I never can forget the three years...

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.590
Rigid discipline...

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:51.459
I was fed like a canary bird... the slices
of ham cut by my aunt were like tissue paper.

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:53.890
I had a voracious appetite...

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:59.390
The land was low and marshy and malaria fever
never left me, while there"

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:04.889
"At last, however, my course was completed,
the misery ended."

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:07.489
That's not a glowing review by Tesla.

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:13.629
After graduation, Tesla's father told him
to go hunting instead of returning home because

00:04:13.629 --> 00:04:16.030
there was a cholera outbreak in the town.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.750
But Tesla returned anyway.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:24.340
And since he was already undernourished and
unwell, he contracted the disease on his very

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.810
first day home and we was bedridden for the
next nine months.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:35.360
This was when Tesla was 17, and at that time
his prospects were to become a priest like

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.389
his father, or to go to the army.

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:40.849
Neither of which he wanted to do.

00:04:40.849 --> 00:04:46.030
When it looked like Tesla might not recover,
his father Milutin promised him that if he

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:50.620
did recover, he could study engineering at
one of the best colleges.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.660
After that, Tesla did make a good recovery
and his father kept his word.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:01.750
For a year after that, Tesla lived in the
mountains with his uncle to fully recover

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.629
and possibly also to avoid conscription into
the army.

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:13.440
Then, two years after he graduated from school,
in 1875, he enrolled at the Austrian polytechnic

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.220
in Graz, where he was to study electrical
engineering.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:26.349
I have his grades from this time at Graz,
and he was there from 1875 to late 1877, which

00:05:26.349 --> 00:05:28.699
was age 19 to 21.

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:33.389
There are two pages to these grades and they're
not in english so they're probably a bit hard

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:37.879
to read, although even if they were in english,
the handwriting makes that difficult.

00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:44.460
You can clearly make out a Nikola Tesla at
the top there, and you can also see his birthday,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.009
the 10th of July, 1856.

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:54.940
He was born in the town of Smiljan, his nationality
is Serbian, this looks like his father's name

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:59.120
in here, and details about the school that
he went to.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.360
In these columns we have the subject, the
lecturer who confirmed the attendance and

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.600
we have the result.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:12.099
Since it's so hard to read, I did make up
a translated version which I'll have here.

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:14.300
And we can have a look at that.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:19.889
We can see that during Tesla's first year
of university he scored all excellents which

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:22.190
is the highest grade possible.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:29.740
In fact, Tesla did so well that he'd done
nearly twice as many exams than is required.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.600
Tesla was really grateful to be there.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:38.340
He said that, "During the whole first year
I regularly started my work at three o'clock

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.669
in the morning and continued until eleven
at night."

00:06:42.669 --> 00:06:49.240
He considered his professors to be very intelligent
and there were three that he particularly liked.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:55.979
These were Roegner who did mathematics, Poeschl
who did experimental physics and Alle, who

00:06:55.979 --> 00:06:57.449
also did mathematics.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:03.220
Tesla said that Alle would often spend hours
with him after a lecture, giving him different

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:08.599
mathematical problems to solve, and it was
he who Tesla showed his first concepts of

00:07:08.599 --> 00:07:11.229
flying machines and turbines to.

00:07:11.229 --> 00:07:16.849
There are some interesting subjects here that
we can look at, for example the cubature of

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:22.090
surfaces, which has got to do with cubes and
finding volumes.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:28.190
And we also have political arithmetic, which
was to do with the statistics of government,

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:34.470
for example how many people lived in a certain
area and how much food did they need.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:40.060
We then have more common things that are pretty
similar to what we do today, maths, physics,

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.800
chemistry, zoology, botany, engineering and
french.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.479
I should note that Tesla says that he didn't
miss any lectures because he considered that

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:51.129
to be a sin and a waste.

00:07:51.129 --> 00:07:56.099
That's in quite a contrast to Einstein who
we covered the grades of recently, who would

00:07:56.099 --> 00:07:59.930
regularly not show up to lectures and prefer
to self study.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:06.009
When Tesla returned home after his first year
of study and showed these grades to his father,

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:08.050
his father kind of dismissed them.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:13.670
But actually years after his father's death,
Nikola found a package of letters which the

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:20.050
professors had written to his father, saying
that, "Unless you take Nikola away from the

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:24.139
institution, he will likely be killed through
overwork".

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:29.719
So it seems like Tesla's professors were actually
begging his father to take him out to protect

00:08:29.719 --> 00:08:31.949
Tesla from working too hard.

00:08:31.949 --> 00:08:38.040
I'll show you his second year grades now,
and they are here in the bottom of this first page.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:45.700
They are 1876 to 1877, they're that section
there and also a little bit on the next page,

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.050
this section here.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:52.230
I also have a little translation here as well
for these second year grades.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.330
There's definitely not as many grades here,
and that's because in his second year, Tesla

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:04.170
only enrolled in some of these maths and physics
type classes, which allowed him to spend more

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.590
time in the library studying.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:12.000
We can see that he's got another two excellent
marks in mathematics and physics which is

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:17.860
the highest score possible, and he's got two
goods down here for "on the congruence of

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.340
numbers" and "selected problems of political
arithmetic."

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:27.150
Something interesting did happen in this second
year, and it was in his technical physics

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.360
class with Poeschl.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:34.540
Professor Poeschl one day brought into the
classroom a new machine called the "Gramme

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:41.221
Dynamo", and it was a machine that, when turned
using power, would generate electricity, and

00:09:41.221 --> 00:09:44.800
if you supplied it with electricity, it would
run as a motor.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:51.180
This was a DC or direct current motor of course,
because that's what people were using in the

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:58.250
day, and it required a commutator to work,
which is a set of wire brushes that convert

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:01.420
an alternating current into being a direct
current.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:05.530
They switch the connection every half cycle.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:10.530
Tesla mentions in his autobiography that during
this demonstration, the machine was sparking

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.220
and creating loud noises.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:17.950
Tesla then got the idea that the commutators
were perhaps not necessary.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:23.850
He gave this opinion to Poeschl, who wasn't
very receptive to the idea, and he lectured

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:30.120
Tesla on why he was wrong, and why his idea
of alternating currents would never work.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:36.960
He said that an AC generator would be a perpetual
motion scheme and an impossible idea.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:42.120
Tesla just had to accept it at the time but
he definitely wasn't convinced.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.810
And later he went on to prove Poeschl wrong.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:52.460
In fact Poeschl is remembered today, mainly
for this very wrong stance in his discussion with Tesla.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:11:02.100
In his third year which was 1877-1878 Tesla
was supposed to take subjects such as Applied

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:10.230
mathematics, mathematics 3 B, Determinant
Theory, Theory of conic sections,

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.230
Analytical mechanics.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:17.550
But instead there is just a note here that
says not reported to the professors.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:22.390
So Tesla hasn't taken any exams in his third
year and instead there's a note at the bottom

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:29.120
saying that his studies have been cancelled
due to a non-payment of tuition fees for the

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.010
first semester 1877/78.

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:40.660
So Tesla started off so well in his studies
but by third year everything had turned to custard.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.780
Now there's a few things that were going on.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:50.740
Tesla had been on a military scholarship which
gave him payment for 3 years in exchange for

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.960
8 years of service in the army afterwards.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:12:00.020
But at the end of his second year he lost this scholarship and it's not exactly clear why.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:04.640
He asked for help from a different organisation
but was twice refused.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:08.610
At the end of his second year he also got
involved in gambling.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:14.500
he would play things like cards, chess and
pool at the botanical gardens all night.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:19.970
And his life became consumed with games and
excessive coffee drinking and he spent less

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.770
time in the library.

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:26.980
Tesla never graduated from university but
he did go on to be awarded several honorary

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:29.470
degrees later in his life.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:35.130
After dropping out he worked for a bit as
a technician, he played a lot of cards and

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.670
he was also was suffering from a nervous breakdown.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:43.130
He was struggling with sensitivity to noise
and light.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:48.630
He said he could hear the ticking of a watch
with three rooms between him and the timepiece.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:53.230
A fly landing on a table would cause a dull
thud in his ear.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:13:00.180
A few years later Tesla did try to finish
his studies and in 1880 he went to study in

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:06.310
Prague but he arrived too late to enrol in
the course and ended up just sitting in on

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:07.930
some of the lectures.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:13.110
There is so much more to say about Tesla that
I don't have time for in this video.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:18.300
He worked more as a technician, he moved to
America and then worked for Thomas Edison

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:21.430
but quit over a dispute about pay.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:27.170
Edison then launched a negative campaign against
him and the two became enemies.

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:33.070
Teslas work and inventions led him to become
the master of lightning.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:39.430
He had a lot of big dreams but lost investment
in trying to build his Wardenclyffe tower

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:42.360
to try supply the world with wireless power.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:48.680
He then sought company in the friendship of 
pigeons and died alone in his New York hotel room.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.960
More videos would be needed to cover all of
that but I hope that this one has given you

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:59.200
a little bit of insight into his early years
and his time as a student.

